{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Plan-review v2 returned BLOCK (G6 case-fold) — remediated, re-review launched\n\n**Blocking finding (G6):** the plan's step-1 pseudocode wrote `{kind for … _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS if not counted}` WITHOUT `.lower()`. Since `_DIRTY_LINE_SPECS` kinds are UPPERCASE (`TRACKER_DIRTY_TMP_EVENT`) but `_transform_json` matches against the lowercased `item['kind']`, a literal implementation of that pseudocode would leave `tracker_dirty_tmp_event` never matched → wrongly `counted=True`, re-inflating the very count being fixed. (My committed CODE already had `kind.lower()`, and the per-kind tmp_event test passed — but the PLAN TEXT was inaccurate, which is what the gate reviews.)\n\n**Remediation:**\n- Corrected the plan pseudocode to `{kind.lower() for … if not counted}` and documented that the whole `_NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS` union is lowercase to match the stamping site.\n- Strengthened the drift guard with an explicit CASE-FOLD SEAM test (`test_case_fold_seam_uppercase_spec_kind_is_not_counted`) that feeds each dirty class's RAW UPPERCASE kind through `_transform_json` and asserts `counted=False`, plus an assertion that every kind in the constant is lowercase. Mutation-verified: removing `.lower()` from the derivation turns 5 held-out tests RED (incl. the new seam test).\n\n**Advisories addressed:**\n- **G1G2:** plan step 6 now explicitly enumerates `test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py:128` (pins the OLD `issue_count == len(issues) >= 1`) and documents WHY it stays green — `unsigned_env` is a COUNTED kind, so the counted subset equals `len(issues)` in that single-finding case (regression-swept).\n- **E6/T5e:** documented the residual inline-scan-kind drift surface — `warn` is structural (drift-proof by construction), the two named inline kinds are guarded by per-kind tests + pointer comments, and a NEW untested inline is_issue=False kind defaults to `counted=True` (the integrity-safe direction).\n\nHeld-out file now: 15 tests pass. Re-running `review-plan`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787958216683851001,"uuid":"2b39edba-6476-42cc-a91d-1cf5a4ae4aea"}